IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 12A -- Forms (ss 48 and 48A).

§ `Part 12A -- Forms`

§§ `s 48 -- Forms: notification and availability`

-- src:929 | (1) This section applies if under an Act (the authorising law) forms are to be approved or made available by an entity.
@ref s 48(1) (src:929-929)
GIVEN `under an Act (the authorising law) forms are to be approved or made available by an entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 48 applies (s 48(1))` IS
    IF `under an Act (the authorising law) forms are to be approved or made available by an entity` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): a form must have a heading stating the name of the authorising law and briefly indicating the form's purpose.
-- The rule answers whether the requirement is met; the text does not say what follows if it is not.
-- src:930 | (2) A form under the authorising law must have a heading stating the name of the authorising law and briefly indicating the form’s purpose.
@ref s 48(2) (src:930-930)
GIVEN `the form has a heading stating the name of the authorising law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the heading briefly indicates the form's purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the form meets the requirement for a heading (s 48(2))` IS
    JUST (`the form has a heading stating the name of the authorising law` AND `the heading briefly indicates the form's purpose`)

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every number in the list is different from the others` MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (NOT (elem x rest)) AND `every number in the list is different from the others` rest

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`each number in the list is one more than the one before` MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER rest
        WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
        WHEN y FOLLOWED BY more THEN (y EQUALS x + 1) AND `each number in the list is one more than the one before` rest

-- (3): all forms must be numbered using a system that gives each form a unique number.
-- src:931 | (3) All forms under the authorising law must be numbered using a system that gives each form a unique number.
@ref s 48(3) (src:931-931)
GIVEN `the numbers given to the forms` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the forms are numbered using a system that gives each form a unique number (s 48(3))` IS
    JUST (`every number in the list is different from the others` `the numbers given to the forms`)

-- (4): all versions of a form must be numbered consecutively using a system that gives each version a unique number.
-- src:935 | (4) All versions of a form under the authorising law must be numbered consecutively using a system that gives each version of the form a unique number.
@ref s 48(4) (src:935-935)
GIVEN `the numbers given to the versions of the form, in order` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the versions of the form are numbered consecutively using a system that gives each version a unique number (s 48(4))` IS
    JUST (   `each number in the list is one more than the one before` `the numbers given to the versions of the form, in order`
         AND `every number in the list is different from the others` `the numbers given to the versions of the form, in order`)

-- src:936 | (5) The approval or availability under the authorising law of a form, or a new version of a form, must be notified in the gazette or on a relevant website.
@ref s 48(5) (src:936-936)
GIVEN `notified in the gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notified on a relevant website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the approval or availability of the form is notified as s 48(5) requires (s 48(5))` IS
    JUST (`notified in the gazette` OR `notified on a relevant website`)

-- (6): subsection (5) may be complied with by publishing in the gazette or on a relevant website or a related website the form or the new version, or a notice stating
-- (A) the approval or availability, (B) the heading, number and version number, (C) the place or places where copies are available; and (b) if on a website, stating the date first published.
-- "May be complied with by": a sufficient way; another way is not answered.
-- src:937 | (6) Subsection (5) may be complied with by—
-- src:938 | (a) publishing in the gazette or on a relevant website or a website (a related website) accessible through the relevant website—
-- src:939 | (i) the form or the new version; or
-- src:940 | (ii) a notice stating—
-- src:941 | (A) the approval or availability of the form or the new version; and
-- src:942 | (B) the heading, number and version number of the form or the new version; and
-- src:943 | (C) a place or places where copies of the form or the new version are available; and
-- src:944 | (b) if the form or the new version, or the notice, is published on a relevant website or a related website—stating on the website the date on which it is first published.
@ref s 48(6) (src:937-944)
GIVEN `published in the gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `published on a relevant website or a related website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is published is the form or the new version` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is published is a notice stating the approval or availability, the heading, number and version number, and the place or places where copies are available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which it is first published is stated on the website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (5) is complied with (s 48(6))` IS
    IF    (`published in the gazette` OR `published on a relevant website or a related website`)
       AND (`what is published is the form or the new version` OR `what is published is a notice stating the approval or availability, the heading, number and version number, and the place or places where copies are available`)
       AND (IF `published on a relevant website or a related website` THEN `the date on which it is first published is stated on the website` ELSE TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:945 | (7) On the day the approval or availability of the form is notified or as soon as practicable after the day, copies of the form must be available (for purchase or free of charge) at the place, or each of the places, stated in the notice.
@ref s 48(7) (src:945-945)
GIVEN `copies of the form are available at the place or each of the places stated in the notice on the day the approval or availability is notified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `copies are available as soon as practicable after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requirement for copies to be available is met (s 48(7))` IS
    JUST (`copies of the form are available at the place or each of the places stated in the notice on the day the approval or availability is notified` OR `copies are available as soon as practicable after that day`)

-- src:946 | (8) Failure to comply with this section does not affect a form’s validity.
@ref s 48(8) (src:946-946)
GIVEN `a person fails to comply with s 48` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the failure to comply affects the form's validity (s 48(8))` IS
    IF `a person fails to comply with s 48` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:947 | (9) In this section—
-- src:948 | relevant department, in relation to an entity that approves or makes available forms under an authorising law, means the department in which the authorising law is administered.
@ref s 48(9), definition relevant department (src:947-948)
GIVEN `the department is the department in which the authorising law is administered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the department is the relevant department (s 48(9), definition relevant department)` IS
    JUST `the department is the department in which the authorising law is administered`

DECLARE `Website` IS ONE OF
    `the local government's website`
    `the whole-of-government website`
    `the entity's website`
    `the relevant department's website`
    `a website identified on the relevant department's website as a website for this purpose`
    `another website`

-- relevant website means (a) for a local government -- the local government's website; (b) for another entity -- (i) the whole-of-government website; or (ii) the entity's website; or
-- (iii) if the entity does not have a website -- (A) the relevant department's website; or (B) a website identified on the relevant department's website as a website for this purpose.
-- src:949 | relevant website means—
-- src:950 | (a) for publication in relation to a form, or a new version of a form, approved or made available by a local government—the local government’s website; or
-- src:951 | (b) for publication in relation to a form, or a new version of a form, approved or made available by another entity—
-- src:952 | (i) the whole-of-government website; or
-- src:953 | (ii) the entity’s website; or
-- src:954 | (iii) if the entity does not have a website—
-- src:955 | (A) the relevant department’s website; or
-- src:956 | (B) a website identified on the relevant department’s website as a website for this purpose.
@ref s 48(9), definition relevant website (src:949-956)
GIVEN `the entity is a local government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity has a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      website IS A `Website`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the website is a relevant website (s 48(9), definition relevant website)` IS
    IF `the entity is a local government`
    THEN JUST (website EQUALS `the local government's website`)
    ELSE CONSIDER website
        WHEN `the whole-of-government website` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the entity's website` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the relevant department's website` THEN JUST (NOT `the entity has a website`)
        WHEN `a website identified on the relevant department's website as a website for this purpose` THEN JUST (NOT `the entity has a website`)
        WHEN `the local government's website` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `another website` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:957 | whole-of-government website means—
-- src:958 | (a) www.qld.gov.au; or
-- src:959 | (b) another website prescribed by regulation.
@ref s 48(9), definition whole-of-government website (src:957-959)
GIVEN `the website address` IS A STRING
      `it is another website prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the website is the whole-of-government website (s 48(9), definition whole-of-government website)` IS
    JUST (`the website address` EQUALS "www.qld.gov.au" OR `it is another website prescribed by regulation`)

§§ `s 48A -- Compliance with forms`

-- src:961 | (1) If a form is prescribed or approved under an Act, strict compliance with the form is not necessary and substantial compliance is sufficient.
@ref s 48A(1) (src:961-961)
GIVEN `a form is prescribed or approved under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `strict compliance with the form is necessary (s 48A(1))` IS FALSE

-- src:961 | (1) If a form is prescribed or approved under an Act, strict compliance with the form is not necessary and substantial compliance is sufficient.
@ref s 48A(1) (src:961-961)
GIVEN `a form is prescribed or approved under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `compliance with the form is substantial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `substantial compliance with the form is sufficient (s 48A(1))` IS
    IF `a form is prescribed or approved under an Act` AND `compliance with the form is substantial` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): "the form is not properly completed unless the requirement is complied with": complying is necessary, and the subsection does not say it is sufficient.
-- src:962 | (2) If a form prescribed or approved under an Act requires—
-- src:963 | (a) the form to be completed in a specified way; or
-- src:964 | (b) specified information or documents to be included in, attached to or given with the form; or
-- src:965 | (c) the form, or information or documents included in, attached to or given with the form, to be verified in a specified way;
-- src:966 | the form is not properly completed unless the requirement is complied with.
@ref s 48A(2) (src:962-966)
GIVEN `the form requires it to be completed in a specified way, or specified information or documents to be included in, attached to or given with it, or it or its contents to be verified in a specified way` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the form is properly completed (s 48A(2))` IS
    IF `the form requires it to be completed in a specified way, or specified information or documents to be included in, attached to or given with it, or it or its contents to be verified in a specified way` AND (NOT `the requirement is complied with`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:967 | (3) If—
-- src:968 | (a) a form (form 1) may be prescribed or approved under an Act for a purpose or 2 or more purposes; and
-- src:969 | (b) another form (form 2) may be prescribed or approved under the Act or another Act for the same or another purpose or purposes;
-- src:970 | then, if separate forms 1 and 2 are prescribed or approved, a combined form 1 and 2 may be prescribed or approved and used for the purpose or all the purposes.
@ref s 48A(3) (src:967-970)
GIVEN `a form (form 1) may be prescribed or approved under an Act for a purpose or 2 or more purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another form (form 2) may be prescribed or approved under the Act or another Act for the same or another purpose or purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `separate forms 1 and 2 are prescribed or approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a combined form 1 and 2 may be prescribed or approved and used for the purpose or all the purposes (s 48A(3))` IS
    IF `a form (form 1) may be prescribed or approved under an Act for a purpose or 2 or more purposes` AND `another form (form 2) may be prescribed or approved under the Act or another Act for the same or another purpose or purposes` AND `separate forms 1 and 2 are prescribed or approved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): the form "may only require" information or documents that are reasonably necessary for the purpose or 1 or more of the purposes.
-- src:971 | (4) If a form may be prescribed or approved under an Act for a purpose or 2 or more purposes, the form may only require information or documents to be included in, attached to or given with the form that are reasonably necessary for the purpose or 1 or more of the purposes.
@ref s 48A(4) (src:971-971)
GIVEN `the information or documents are reasonably necessary for the purpose or 1 or more of the purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the form may require the information or documents to be included in, attached to or given with the form (s 48A(4))` IS
    JUST `the information or documents are reasonably necessary for the purpose or 1 or more of the purposes`
